  "job_B3.4.1_20251003_114729": {
    "text": "Men \u00fea leofest\u00e6, we wull\u00e6\u00f0 eow s\u00e6gg\u00e6n bi \u00feare halg\u00e6 tide \u00fee nu toweard is, \u00fee we onsundren mare\nHit is iwriten \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee H\u00e6lend son\u00e6 \u00e6fter his fuluhte ferde on sume w\u00e6sten & \u00fe\u00e6r fest\u00e6 feowertig dage\nNe f\u00e6ste he na for\u00fean \u00f0\u00e6t he \u00e6fre \u00e6nig sunne wrohte \u00fe\u00e6t he mid \u00feam festen beten \u00feurfte.\nAc he feste \u00fe\u00e6t he walde monncynnes sunn\u00e6n h\u00e6len & ales\u00e6n, & us bisne onst\u00e6ll\u00e6n, \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6 witen \u00fe\u00e6t\nCrist \u00feolede eac on \u00feam w\u00e6sten \u00feene awarigede deofel hine fandi\u00e6n, swa we nu her\u00e6fter secg\u00e6n\nSanctus Matheus wrat, \u00fee godspellere, \u00feis d\u00e6g\u00feerlice godspel \u00e6fter \u00feissere endeburdnesse, \u00feus\nDuctus est Ihesus in desertum a Spiritu ut temptaretur a diabolo. He cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fee H\u00e6lend w\u00e6s il\u00e6d fram\nMonie men tweoni\u00e6\u00f0 fram hwylce gaste Crist w\u00e6re on \u00fe\u00e6t westen il\u00e6d, nu hit swa cu\u00f0lice on \u00feissum\nHit is buton tweon to lyfen & geare to witenne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0e Halige Gast him wunsumlice on \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6sten\nNa for \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee deofel h\u00e6fde \u00e6nig fare to ure H\u00e6lende o\u00f0er his m\u00e6\u00f0 w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t he him ahw\u00e6r on\nAc he hit dude ure life to bisene \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6lde \u00fe\u00e6t we wisten hu ea\u00f0elice he \u00feene deofel ofercom na\nSwa eac nu m\u00e6g ealc mon deofel ofercumen, gif he on rihtwisnesse & on gode weorcum his lif adrih\u00f0.\n\u00d0a son\u00e6 \u00fea \u00f0e H\u00e6lend on \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6sten becom, \u00fea f\u00e6ste he feowertig daga & nihte tog\u00e6dere; & \u00e6fter\nWiterlice on \u00feam hit w\u00e6s fulcu\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6fde so\u00f0ne lichame \u00fea him hingri\u00e6n mihte.\nHit is iwriten on \u00feare ealde lage \u00fe\u00e6t tw\u00e6ge men herbiforen \u00feis festen festen.\nMoyses feste feowertig dage & nihte togedere \u00fea he w\u00e6s on Synai \u00fe\u00e6re dune \u00e6t Drihtines spece; &\nElias \u00fee witeg\u00e6 feste eac \u00fe\u00e6t ilce festen feowertig dage & niht\u00e6 tosomne, \u00e6fter \u00fean \u00f0e he \u00e6t \u00feigede\n& \u00e6fter \u00feam f\u00e6sten he wear\u00f0 mid wisdomes gaste ifulled, & him \u00fea toweard\u00e6n \u00feing unwreah &\nNu eft on \u00feis ytemeste tide \u00fee H\u00e6lend hine eadmedede to \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feis ylce f\u00e6sten feste feowertig\u00e6\nFor hwon nolde \u00fee deofel fanden Moysen & Heliam swa he ure H\u00e6lend fondode, buten for \u00feon \u00f0e he\nFor n\u00e6s n\u00e6fr\u00e6 nan mon on \u00feisse midd\u00e6nearde swa halig, \u00fe\u00e6t he on summe \u00feinge ne sunegode buten\nAc \u00fea \u00f0e deofel com to him, \u00fea iseah he \u00fe\u00e6t he h\u00e6fde so\u00f0ne lichame & \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s unilic \u00e6lle o\u00f0re\n\u00dea ondredde \u00fee deofel \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re swa swa hit w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s lifiende Godes Sune, & \u00feohte \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t he\nBer \u00fea to him \u00fea ylce costung\u00e6 \u00fee he \u00fea ereste men Adam & Euam mid forcostode & biswaac, & his\n\u00dea wolde Crist \u00feone awariede deofel ofercumen on \u00feam ylce \u00ferem costunge \u00fee \u00f0e deofel \u00e6r \u00fea ereste\n\u00d0a neahl\u00e6chede \u00fee deofel to \u00feam H\u00e6lende & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Gyf \u00feu eart Godes Sune, hat \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6s\nN\u00e6s Criste nan earfo\u00f0nesse \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fea stanes mid his worde to lafes wrohte; for gif he hit icw\u00e6de, hit\n\u00dea nolde \u00fea gyt Crist haten \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a stanes to lafes wur\u00f0en, ac he walde \u00fe\u00e6t his godcundlice miht w\u00e6re\nHw\u00e6t we witen \u00fe\u00e6t monnes lichame sceal bi mete libban, \u00fea hwile \u00fee he on \u00feisse life bi\u00f0; swa sceal\n\u00d0a nam \u00fee deofel \u00feene H\u00e6lend on \u00fe\u00e6re halgan burig & sette hine ofer \u00fe\u00e6s temples yppan \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6re\nHit \u00feunc\u00fe monige monnum wunderlice to herenne, & eac unea\u00f0elic to lyfene, hu deofel \u00e6fre \u00fea\nEal\u00e6.\nGif we wull\u00e6\u00fe i\u00feencean his o\u00f0re d\u00e6de \u00fee mucele mare & eadmodlicre beo\u00f0, \u00feenne mage we \u00feisses \u00fee\nCrist is alle halige monn\u00e6 heafod, & alle halige men beo\u00f0 his limen: & deofel is eac alle synfulle\nSo\u00f0lice \u00fea Iudeus w\u00e6ren alle deofles limen, \u00fea \u00f0\u00e6 ure H\u00e6lend to dea\u00fee demdon.\nPilatus w\u00e6s eac deofles lim, \u00fee \u00f0e ure Drihten lichamlice ahon h\u00e6t.\nHwylc wunder w\u00e6s \u00feenne \u00feeah Crist \u00f0a durstinesse deofle sealde \u00fe\u00e6t he his lichame rin\u00e6n moste, \u00fea\nEal\u00e6.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s mucele mare & eadmodlicre \u00feonne \u00fe\u00e6s deofles \u00e6trine, & he hit \u00feeah for monn\u00e6 h\u00e6le\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee deofel to Criste, Gif \u00feu eard Godes Sune, \u00feenne asend \u00feu nu \u00fee adun of \u00feissere uppon: for\nOn \u00feesne \u00e6nne godspel we r\u00e6d\u00e6\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t deofel ongan halige bec to reccan, ah he \u00fea sone \u00feone forme\nN\u00e6s hit n\u00e6fre sunderlice bi Criste iseid \u00fe\u00e6t him sceoldon engl\u00e6s on fultume cumen: ac hit w\u00e6s\nFor \u00fean \u00fee engl\u00e6s beo\u00f0 heom on fultume h\u00e6r on weorlde; & \u00e6ft \u00feenne heo of \u00feisse lif\u00e6 far\u00e6\u00f0, \u00feonne\n\u00d0a andswerede Crist \u00feam awarigede gaste & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Hit is iwriten, \u00fe\u00e6t mon ne sceal\nHw\u00e6t.\nCrist mihte ea\u00f0e mid ane worde \u00feenne deofel senden on ece lure, gif he him his godcund\u00e6n mihte\nAc he us \u00fea bysene onstealde \u00fe\u00e6t we sceolon yfelr\u00e6 mann\u00e6 hate & heora ni\u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0uldelice forber\u00e6n, &\nEft \u00fee deofel nam \u00feonne H\u00e6lend & l\u00e6dde hine on ane swi\u00f0e heahne dune & sceawede him alles\nWiterlice n\u00e6s Criste nohte wur\u00f0 \u00feisses middeneardes rices ne \u00feysses witigend\u00e6n wuldres \u00feissere\nAc \u00fee deofel h\u00e6fde \u00feeah mid leasunge \u00feurh his syncrefte middaneardes murh\u00fee & all weorldlice\n\u00deeah hit \u00f0enne allung\u00e6 mon w\u00e6re \u00fee him \u00fe\u00e6re wi\u00f0 speke, \u00feenne mihte he \u00feeah alle weorldlice\nHwilon he sceaw\u00e6\u00f0 hine seluen on engles hywe & bi\u00f0 \u00feeahwe\u00f0ere awariged gast swa swa he \u00e6r w\u00e6s.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee deofel to Criste, Alle \u00feas \u00f0ing ic \u00fee gyfe & sylle, gyf \u00feu wult fallen to mine fotum &\nEl\u00e6.\nHw\u00e6t \u00e6lc \u00feare monn\u00e6 sarlice gefalle\u00f0 \u00fee hine nu to deofle geeadmode\u00fe.\nNis nan mon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6fre \u00feam deofle georne ihyre, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00e6ft \u00e6t him \u00fee b\u00e6tere are finden mage; ac \u00e6fre\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Crist to \u00feam deofle, Ga heonne on hinderling, \u00feu awariged\u00e6 sceocc\u00e6; so\u00f0lice hit is iwrit\u00e6n;\n\u00dea sy\u00f0\u00e6n weron deofles miht\u00e6 on hinderling afulled, & Cristes lare w\u00e6s a sy\u00f0\u00e6n waxende geond\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t mon sceal to Gode Almihtig ane biddan & him ane \u00feeowian.\nSo\u00f0lice ne sceole we us bidd\u00e6n na\u00feor ne to englum ne to o\u00fere halige monnum, buton to ure Drihtne\nAc we sceolen \u00feeah \u00e6lcne Godes halge bidd\u00e6n to fultume, & to \u00feingunge, & \u00feeahhw\u00e6\u00fere to nan o\u00f0re\n\u00d0a forlet \u00fee deofel \u00feene H\u00e6lend & aw\u00e6g awat; & engles him sone neahl\u00e6cedon & him seruedon.\nOn \u00feis we magen openlice undergyten ure H\u00e6lendes cynde, \u00fe\u00e6t he is \u00e6g\u00f0er ge so\u00f0 God ge so\u00f0 mon.\nIwislice ne durste \u00fee deofel fondien hine, gif he ful geare ne cneow\u00e6 \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6re so\u00f0 mon; ne eac\nOfte si\u00fe\u00e6s hit ilamp, & nu gyt de\u00fe, \u00fe\u00e6t engl\u00e6s beo\u00f0 ofte hyder on middanearde isende, monnum to\nBe \u00feam cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee apostol, Engl\u00e6s beo\u00f0 \u00feeiniendlice gastes; & heo beo\u00f0 hider on middanearde isende\nMucel is \u00feeo wur\u00f0scipe \u00fee God Almihtig us haf\u00f0 igyfen, gif we moten beon his bearn icw\u00e6dene &\nUten gemunen hu \u00fee apostol us munede & t\u00e6hte & l\u00e6rde, & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, Nu is \u00fee anfenge tid, & nu\nNe sceole we nenne mon bylgen, l\u00e6s \u00fee ure bene ne beo noht; ac on alle \u00feinge gearwie we us sylfe\n\u00deas m\u00e6gnu werces l\u00e6de\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6s monnes sawle on heofene rice \u00fee heom on him h\u00e6f\u00f0.\nSo\u00f0lice hit w\u00e6s iboden & ihaten on \u00feare ealde \u00e6 \u00fe\u00e6t ylc mon sceolde \u00e6fre embe twelf mon\u00f0e \u00feone\nGif hit \u00feonne hwylcum men on his mode to earfo\u00felic & to unea\u00feelic \u00feynce, tylie he \u00fe\u00e6t he hyre \u00feone\nHw\u00e6t we witen \u00fe\u00e6t on twelf mon\u00fee beo\u00f0 \u00fereo hundred dag\u00e6 & fif & sixtig dage, & six tid\u00e6; & \u00feisses\nSwa hwylc mon swa wule on ylce tid heardlice & forwyrnedlice libb\u00e6n, \u00fee bi\u00f0 fulfremed.\nGyf hit \u00feonne hwylcum men to earfo\u00felice \u00feince, tilie he \u00feenne \u00fe\u00e6t he hure \u00feis f\u00e6sten selost feste,\nAMEN.",
